SUMMARY:Middle Creek Winter Bird Walk
DESCRIPTION:This field trip offers a hands-on birding experience that will allow participants to explore Middle Creek’s winter landscape and observe the season’s local bird species while gaining insight into the process of counting birds for the Christmas Bird Count (CBC). Whether you’re a seasoned birder or new to birding and CBCs\, this outing offers a unique opportunity to connect with nature and learn how birding data is collected in the field each year for this citizen-science survey. Pre-registration is required by 5 p.m the day prior for this offering. Contact Ted at tanicholsii@gmail.com or 717-856-3851 if you have questions or want to make a reservation to attend. \nIMPORTANT NOTE: Attendees must wear blaze orange for this field trip per new Pennsylvania Game Commission regulations requiring wear on Game Lands Oct. 1 through Jan. 31. \n\nLocation: Middle Creek Wildlife Management Area Visitor Center\, 100 Museum Road\, Stevens\, PA 17578 \nContact: Ted Nichols\, 717-856-3851 or tanicholsii@gmail.com.
URL:https://lancasterbirdclub.org/event/middle-creek-winter-walk/
LOCATION:Middle Creek Wildlife Management Area Visitor Center\, 100 Museum Road\, Stevens\, PA\, 17578\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://lancasterbirdclub.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/IMG_0575.jpeg
END:VEVENT
